-- title:
--   Regular sequence generating 𝔪 forces freeness
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring that is local and Noetherian, and let $rs = [r_1,\dots,r_n]$ be a finite list of elements of $A$. Assume two things about $rs$ as a sequence on $A$ itself: it is a regular sequence, in the sense of `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs`, i.e. each $r_i$ acts injectively on $A/(r_1,\dots,r_{i-1})$ and the final quotient $A/(r_1,\dots,r_n)$ is nonzero; and the ideal `Ideal.ofList rs` generated by the entries of the list is exactly the maximal ideal `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`. Let $M$ be an $A$-module that is finite (finitely generated) over $A$, and assume that the same list $rs$ is a regular sequence on $M$, i.e. each $r_i$ acts injectively on $M/(r_1,\dots,r_{i-1})M$ and $M/(r_1,\dots,r_n)M \neq 0$. The conclusion is that $M$ is a free $A$-module. No rank is asserted, and the length $n$ of the list is arbitrary, so the statement applies uniformly in all dimensions (including $n = 0$, where $A$ is a field).
--
--   The hypotheses on $A$ say that $r_1,\dots,r_n$ is a regular system of parameters, so $A$ is regular local of dimension $n$, and the condition on $M$ says that the depth of $M$ equals $n$; the conclusion is the direction of the Auslander–Buchsbaum theorem asserting that a maximal-depth finite module over a regular local ring is free. It serves in this development as the criterion for freeness, and hence flatness, of stalks and of modules of sections on integral models of modular curves, being used by the flatness and finite-rank statements for those models.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_free_of_isRegular_of_span_eq_maximalIdeal.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem Module.free_of_isRegular_of_span_eq_maximalIdeal
    {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (rs : List A) (hA : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs) (hspan : Ideal.ofList rs = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module.Finite A M] (hM : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M rs) :
    Module.Free A M := by sorry
